{#
mail/_message_body.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
One message body, and everything that has to be true around it.

Included from the conversation view, the single-message pane and the trust
Turbo Stream — so it owns the id those three agree on.

WHY THE BODY IS IN AN IFRAME
────────────────────────────
It used to be injected straight into the app's own DOM. MailBodySanitizer held
— nothing got through it — but "the sanitizer has no gaps" is a claim that has
to keep being true forever, against every sender, and the cost of it being
wrong once was a same-origin script with the session cookie. In here a gap is
worth nothing: no allow-same-origin means an opaque origin, which has no access
to our cookies, our storage or this document. The second thing it buys is
smaller but hits every day — a sender's `td { padding: 0 }` can no longer
reach the application's own layout.

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *OUTSIDE* THE FRAME
────────────────────────────────────────
Every warning, and the images bar. A banner rendered inside the sandbox is a
banner mail markup can draw for itself, and a "Show images" button the message
can forge is worse than no button at all. The trust boundary and the visual
boundary are the same line.

Variables:
  message  Message
#}
{% set render = message_render(message) %}

<div id="message_body_{{ message.id }}" class="mail-message-body">

    {# ── Warnings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if render.inSpam %}
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 px-3 py-2.5 mb-3"
             data-testid="spam-warning">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-danger mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-danger">{{ 'message.security.spam.title'|trans }}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ 'message.security.spam.body'|trans }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if render.mismatch is not null %}
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 px-3 py-2.5 mb-3"
             data-testid="sender-mismatch-warning">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield text-warning mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'message.security.mismatch.title'|trans }}</p>
                {# Shows its working: the claim, and the address it came from.
                   A reader can disagree with a fact; they can only obey a verdict. #}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted break-words">
                    {{ render.mismatch.kind.translationKey|trans({
                        '%claimed%': render.mismatch.claimed,
                        '%actual%':  render.mismatch.actual,
                    }) }}
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── The reading frame ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if render.content.html is not empty %}

        {% set frameDocument %}<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="{{ render.csp }}">
{# Every link in a mail body opens away from the app. MailBodySanitizer already
   forces target="_blank" per link; this covers anything it did not author. #}
<base target="_blank">
<style>
    /* The mail sheet, carried across the document boundary.
       CSS custom properties do not inherit into a frame, and an opaque-origin
       frame cannot be reached from outside to be styled — so these are the
       fallbacks that paint immediately, and the parent controller posts the
       live theme values over the top as soon as it can read them. Every theme's
       sheet is light (see app.css), so a light default is never far wrong and
       there is no flash of the wrong colours. */
    :root { color-scheme: light; }
    html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body {
        background: #fff;
        color: #27272a;
        font: 14px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
        word-break: break-word;
        overflow-x: auto;
    }
    a { color: #1d4ed8; }
    /* Senders assume a viewport. Without this a 700px table adds a horizontal
       scrollbar to a pane that used to just show it. */
    img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
    /* A blocked image keeps its box so the layout holds, and says so. */
    img[data-plmail-blocked] {
        min-width: 12px; min-height: 12px;
        background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #f4f4f5 0 6px, #e4e4e7 6px 12px);
        outline: 1px dashed #a1a1aa;
        outline-offset: -1px;
    }
</style>
</head><body>
{{ render.content.html|raw }}
<script nonce="{{ render.nonce }}">
(function () {
    "use strict";
    // This script is the ONLY script that can run in here. `script-src
    // 'nonce-…'` in the CSP above means markup arriving in an email cannot
    // execute even if it somehow survived the sanitizer — it has no nonce, and
    // it cannot read this one, because reading it would require running.
    var send = function (message) { parent.postMessage(message, "*"); };

    var lastHeight = -1;
    var reportHeight = function (force) {
        var height = Math.max(
            document.body.scrollHeight,
            document.documentElement.scrollHeight
        );
        if (force || height !== lastHeight) { lastHeight = height; send({ plmail: "height", height: height }); }
    };

    window.addEventListener("load", reportHeight);
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", reportHeight);
    // Images settle after layout, and a mail is mostly images.
    window.addEventListener("resize", reportHeight);
    if (window.ResizeObserver) { new ResizeObserver(reportHeight).observe(document.documentElement); }

    // Link preview. Detected in here because this is where the links are;
    // DRAWN by the parent, because a status bar the message could paint over
    // is a status bar that can lie about where a link goes.
    document.addEventListener("mouseover", function (event) {
        var anchor = event.target && event.target.closest ? event.target.closest("a[href]") : null;
        if (anchor) { send({ plmail: "link", href: anchor.href }); }
    });
    document.addEventListener("mouseout", function (event) {
        var anchor = event.target && event.target.closest ? event.target.closest("a[href]") : null;
        if (anchor) { send({ plmail: "link", href: null }); }
    });

    window.addEventListener("message", function (event) {
        // The parent is the only window that can reach us.
        if (event.source !== parent || !event.data || typeof event.data !== "object") { return; }

        // A message from the parent is proof its listener is live NOW. This
        // frame's first height report is parsed and sent synchronously, before
        // the parent's Stimulus controller connects — on a full page load the
        // app's module script is deferred — so that first report lands with no
        // listener and is dropped, and the dedupe above then never re-sends the
        // unchanged height. The frame stays at its 80px minimum with the whole
        // message scrolling inside it. The parent asks for a measurement once
        // it is listening; answer it unconditionally.
        if (event.data.plmail === "measure") { reportHeight(true); }

        if (event.data.plmail === "show-images") {
            document.querySelectorAll("img[data-plmail-src]").forEach(function (img) {
                // The stored value is already a proxy URL on our own origin —
                // built server-side. There is no path from here back to the
                // sender's host, whatever this code does.
                img.src = img.getAttribute("data-plmail-src");
                img.removeAttribute("data-plmail-src");
                img.removeAttribute("data-plmail-blocked");
            });
            document.querySelectorAll("[data-plmail-style]").forEach(function (element) {
                element.setAttribute("style", element.getAttribute("data-plmail-style"));
                element.removeAttribute("data-plmail-style");
                element.removeAttribute("data-plmail-blocked");
            });
            reportHeight();
        }

        if (event.data.plmail === "theme" && event.data.vars) {
            var vars = event.data.vars;
            document.body.style.background = vars.sheet || "";
            document.body.style.color = vars.ink || "";
            var rule = document.createElement("style");
            rule.textContent = "a{color:" + (vars.link || "#1d4ed8").replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9(),.%# ]/g, "") + "}";
            document.head.appendChild(rule);
        }
    });

    reportHeight();
})();
</script>
</body></html>{% endset %}

        <div
            data-controller="mail--message-frame"
            data-mail--message-frame-min-height-value="80"
            class="relative"
        >
            <iframe
                data-mail--message-frame-target="frame"
                {# aria-label, not title: the frame still needs an accessible
                   name, but `title` on an iframe is also a browser tooltip, so
                   it popped up "Message content" over the whole body on every
                   hover. aria-label names it for assistive tech and shows
                   nothing on hover. #}
                aria-label="{{ 'message.body_frame'|trans }}"
                sandbox="{{ render.sandbox }}"
                referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
                loading="lazy"
                class="w-full block border-0 bg-transparent"
                style="height: 80px;"
                srcdoc="{{ frameDocument|e('html') }}"
            ></iframe>

            {# The link preview. In the parent, pinned to the frame's corner —
               it reads as part of the frame and cannot be drawn by the mail. #}
            <div
                data-mail--message-frame-target="status"
                class="hidden absolute bottom-0 left-0 max-w-full truncate rounded-tr-md bg-ink/85 text-inverse-ink px-2 py-1 text-[11px] font-mono pointer-events-none z-10"
                data-testid="link-preview"
            ></div>
        </div>
    {% elseif render.text %}
        {# No HTML body: plain text needs no sandbox, because there is no markup
           to sandbox. Twig escapes it, so it is text all the way down. #}
        <pre class="mail-sheet whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-sans text-sm">{{ render.text }}</pre>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── The images bar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if render.offersImages %}
        <div
            class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1.5 mt-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-raised px-3 py-2"
            data-testid="images-bar"
            data-controller="mail--remote-images"
        >
            <i class="fa-regular fa-image text-ink-faint text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted flex-1 min-w-0">
                {{ 'message.images.blocked'|trans({'%count%': render.content.blocked}) }}
            </span>

            <button
                type="button"
                data-action="click->mail--remote-images#show"
                data-testid="show-images"
                class="text-xs font-medium text-link hover:underline"
            >{{ 'message.images.show_once'|trans }}</button>

            {# Only offered where it can be honoured. A message in Spam does not
               load images on an allowlist (see MessageRenderer), so offering to
               add one here would be a button that visibly does nothing. #}
            {% if not render.inSpam %}
                <form
                    method="post"
                    action="{{ path('app_mail_images_trust', {'id': message.id}) }}"
                    data-turbo="true"
                >
                    <button
                        type="submit"
                        data-testid="always-show-images"
                        class="text-xs font-medium text-link hover:underline"
                    >{{ 'message.images.always'|trans({'%sender%': message.fromAddress}) }}</button>
                </form>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if render.senderTrusted and render.content.allowed > 0 %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3 text-xs text-ink-faint" data-testid="images-trusted">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate">
                {{ 'message.images.trusted'|trans({'%sender%': message.fromAddress}) }}
            </span>
            <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_mail_images_distrust', {'id': message.id}) }}" data-turbo="true">
                <button type="submit" class="font-medium text-link hover:underline">
                    {{ 'message.images.stop_trusting'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

</div>
